cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use AnuLM in academic work, please cite it as below."
title: "AnuLM: a small, trainable mixture-of-experts language model, trained from scratch on one GPU for Hindi, English and Python"
type: software
version: 0.2.0
date-released: 2026-09-18
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/MOBIRIZER-TECHNOLOGY/AnuLM"
url: "https://huggingface.co/toonist"
authors:
  - name: "The AnuLM authors"
keywords:
  - mixture-of-experts
  - Hindi
  - Indic languages
  - small language model
  - code generation
  - machine translation
abstract: >-
  AnuLM (अणु, "atom") is a decoder-only mixture-of-experts language model
  (grouped-query attention, 24 routed experts with aux-loss-free
  balancing, sliding-window attention on the lower layers) at roughly 400M
  parameters, 174M active per token, in pure PyTorch. It ships the training,
  evaluation and serving code, the data recipes, and four checkpoints
  trained on a single consumer GPU: a Python coder (MBPP 12.5% pass@1), an
  English-Hindi translator (chrF 41.5 / 43.4 on FLORES-200 devtest), a
  Hindi/English question answerer, and the three-language base model the
  latter two were fine-tuned from. It is an independent project, not
  affiliated with any company or government body.
